    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
This class inherits from :cpp:class:`BaseIniGraphEdit`

Renames `3DMigoto`_ variables everywhere in the `sections`_ of some caller/callee graph of
:cpp:class:`IniSectionGraph`: in each key (``global persist $x``, ``post $x``), each value and each ``if`` /
``else if`` condition. Which ``$name`` count is :cpp:func:`IniNamingTools::varsIn`&apos;s answer -- a namespaced
reference names another file&apos;s variable and is left alone :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

For a `section`_ copied out of another ``.ini`` whose conditions read that file&apos;s own variables: a file with
no ``namespace`` names its variables after its PATH, so another file cannot read them, and the copy reads a
variable of its own under a name no other file uses
</verbatim> <parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>K</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the keys stored in a referenced :cpp:class:<computeroutput><ref refid="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_if_content_part" kindref="compound">IfContentPart</ref></computeroutput> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>V</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the values stored in a referenced :cpp:class:<computeroutput><ref refid="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_if_content_part" kindref="compound">IfContentPart</ref></computeroutput> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>KeyHash</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>A hasher for <computeroutput>K</computeroutput>. Defaults to <computeroutput>std::hash&lt;K&gt;</computeroutput> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>KeyEqual</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>An equality comparator for <computeroutput>K</computeroutput>. Defaults to <computeroutput>std::equal_to&lt;K&gt;</computeroutput> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
